01:06:16,733 --> 01:06:23,115
What if we're on some kind of
physical or metaphysical danger?

458
01:06:24,950 --> 01:06:28,330
Then we don't have any time to waste.

459
01:06:30,373 --> 01:06:34,378
I'm serious.
- So am I.

460
01:06:36,297 --> 01:06:38,799
I'm gonna move a little bit closer, okay.

461
01:06:43,305 --> 01:06:46,600
How come you never
asked me out, Eli?

462
01:06:48,602 --> 01:06:51,439
You always have a boyfriend.

463
01:06:53,358 --> 01:06:55,568
I would've said yes.

464
01:06:55,735 --> 01:07:01,241
You seem to always be with a
guy that look different from me.

465
01:07:04,703 --> 01:07:06,706
Can you forgive me?

466
01:07:14,632 --> 01:07:16,175
I forgive you.

467
01:07:29,190 --> 01:07:33,695
It's gonna be awesome, man.
- Here, put this in your pocket.

468
01:07:33,861 --> 01:07:37,324
And don't let her see it.
- What's wrong?

469
01:07:37,491 --> 01:07:41,286
Maybe she's a big loser like her friend.
- I'm not a loser.

470
01:07:41,453 --> 01:07:46,668
Sandy, I don't feel so good.
- Come on, Sandy. This was your idea.

471
01:07:46,835 --> 01:07:51,381
Yeah, I mean, what's the big deal?
- We're gonna be late for dinner.

472
01:07:51,548 --> 01:07:55,511
Yeah, whuzz.
- Everybody shut up. We're doing this, got it.

473
01:07:58,806 --> 01:08:01,018
Give me the paint.

474
01:08:12,363 --> 01:08:15,616
Easy, easy.

475
01:08:22,791 --> 01:08:25,128
Where did you learn that?

476
01:08:25,295 --> 01:08:28,840
Whatever "that" was.

477
01:08:32,053 --> 01:08:35,056
A gentleman never tells..

478
01:08:35,222 --> 01:08:39,895
Well, a gentleman could never do that either.

479
01:08:40,062 --> 01:08:43,357
Where are you going?
- To get us some drinks.

480
01:08:43,523 --> 01:08:46,777
Give you a chance to recharge.

481
01:08:46,943 --> 01:08:53,493
Let me guess. This is where you disappear
and leave me cold and alone.

482
01:08:53,659 --> 01:08:56,205
Cold? Yes.

483
01:08:57,373 --> 01:08:59,875
Alone? Not a chance.

484
01:09:00,042 --> 01:09:03,046
Oh, just so you don't forget...

485
01:09:12,890 --> 01:09:14,684
It's okay.

486
01:09:17,520 --> 01:09:20,107
Jesus Christ, Sandy.

487
01:09:27,532 --> 01:09:30,410
Sorry, you scared me.
- You see that sign?

488
01:09:30,576 --> 01:09:34,790
You break your neck,
we're ain't accountable.

489
01:09:41,797 --> 01:09:43,925
Oh, creep.

490
01:10:02,112 --> 01:10:05,950
Eli, come here, help me up.
She's gonna hurt herself, hold her up.

491
01:10:13,124 --> 01:10:15,794
Pull her legs.

492
01:10:21,301 --> 01:10:22,802
I saw that mister.

493
01:10:27,515 --> 01:10:30,269
I know you're there, asshole.

494
01:10:32,396 --> 01:10:34,815
Listen perv, don't make me call the...

495
01:11:52,028 --> 01:11:54,196
This isn't real.

496
01:11:57,242 --> 01:11:59,286
This isn't real.

497
01:12:01,288 --> 01:12:03,916
Please, get away.

498
01:12:05,084 --> 01:12:06,836
Please, get away.

499
01:12:40,874 --> 01:12:47,006
There's my girl. I wasn't sure if
you wanted vodka or rhum.

500
01:12:47,173 --> 01:12:49,217
Where is my brother?

501
01:13:01,398 --> 01:13:04,901
Sandy, where the hell are you?
- Eli, are you okay?

502
01:13:05,068 --> 01:13:08,572
No, look, mom and dad are all over me.
I can't cover for you anymore.

503
01:13:08,739 --> 01:13:10,700
Is Hannah with you?

504
01:13:13,536 --> 01:13:17,833
Meet me at the convent, okay.
- Sandy, just come home. Sheriff Mitchell stopped by the house.

505
01:13:17,999 --> 01:13:20,335
Please meet me there.

506
01:13:31,223 --> 01:13:33,308
I thought we're on a hurry.

507
01:14:02,300 --> 01:14:05,428
May I help?
- Sorry to bother you...

508
01:14:05,595 --> 01:14:09,224
I'm Sandy Channing and this is my friend...
- Jake Mitchell.

509
01:14:09,391 --> 01:14:12,519
The quarterback?
- Yes ma'am.

510
01:14:12,686 --> 01:14:18,610
Father Michael and I, we listen
to all the games on the Hi-Fi.

511
01:14:18,777 --> 01:14:22,739
I'm Sister Dolores. Please come in.

512
01:14:25,951 --> 01:14:29,580
I'm sorry sister, I know it's late.
- What can I do for you?

513
01:14:29,747 --> 01:14:32,501
We're here because of Angela Smith.

514
01:14:33,668 --> 01:14:38,423
How do you know her?
- I used to know her when I was little.

515
01:14:38,590 --> 01:14:42,136
Of course.
- Sister, Sandy is just concerned...

516
01:14:42,303 --> 01:14:46,891
Is Angela her?
- Oh, I wish she was...

517
01:14:47,058 --> 01:14:51,021
but it's just not practical,
I'm sure you understand.

518
01:14:51,188 --> 01:14:55,275
Do you know where she might be?
- At St. Mary's hospital.

519
01:14:55,442 --> 01:14:59,656
They're quite wonderful there.
- Is she hurt?

520
01:15:03,243 --> 01:15:05,621
Angela is in coma.

521
01:15:06,747 --> 01:15:11,837
Oh, I'm sorry.
I assumed you knew.

522
01:15:12,003 --> 01:15:13,630
A coma?

523
01:15:15,382 --> 01:15:20,805
Thank you for your time.
- Well, I could show you her room.

524
01:15:25,143 --> 01:15:29,064
I've kept her room just as she's left it.

525
01:15:29,231 --> 01:15:35,071
Her doctors say that her condition
is permanent but well one hopes...

526
01:15:36,364 --> 01:15:41,035
Oh well, the girls' floor...
- Mr. Mitchell can wait down here on the boys' floor.

527
01:15:41,202 --> 01:15:46,917
Can he come with me?
- I'll be fine. I'll stay here on the boys' floor.

528
01:15:48,335 --> 01:15:49,920
Please, come in.
Come in. Come in.

529
01:15:57,345 --> 01:16:02,894
Girls, girls, game time is over.
Ride along.

530
01:16:03,061 --> 01:16:06,982
Say your prayers.
I'll be there and I'll tuck you in a moment.

531
01:16:08,275 --> 01:16:11,779
A little rhyme I teach the children.

532
01:16:13,072 --> 01:16:16,826
It helps to keep the nightmares at bay.

533
01:16:25,836 --> 01:16:31,051
Do you believe in the devil, Mr. Mitchell?
- No, not really.

534
01:16:31,218 --> 01:16:36,348
Well, spend some time with these
little monsters, you'll believe.

535
01:16:37,641 --> 01:16:41,312
So this is Angela's room?

536
01:16:43,147 --> 01:16:47,569
This is a week before
it happened.

537
01:16:47,736 --> 01:16:51,240
Six years ago this June.

538
01:16:51,407 --> 01:16:57,997
How was that possible?
- Oh, I ask the Lord that every day.

539
01:16:59,124 --> 01:17:04,755
Doctors blamed genetics but I don't
know. She was small...

540
01:17:04,922 --> 01:17:08,217
and weaker than
the other children.

541
01:17:08,384 --> 01:17:13,140
But I had faith that
God would protect her.

542
01:17:16,852 --> 01:17:22,650
Angela believed in her own
kind of protection.

543
01:17:24,277 --> 01:17:29,283
An angel?
- Faith is all-powerful.

544
01:17:29,450 --> 01:17:35,540
If one truly believes in something,
one will make it come true.

545
01:17:37,417 --> 01:17:43,424
Of course, we have to be careful
what we choose to believe in.

546
01:17:44,133 --> 01:17:49,055
Duty calls. Forgive me.
I'll be right back.

547
01:17:59,192 --> 01:18:03,738
Hey, you play any football?
- Do I play football?

548
01:18:03,905 --> 01:18:05,741
Toss here, kid.

549
01:18:07,284 --> 01:18:12,165
You see this arm? In Jefferson County,
it's worth more than your life.

550
01:18:15,043 --> 01:18:17,962
Nice arm. For a girl.

551
01:18:19,047 --> 01:18:20,966
Kid, hey kid.

552
01:18:47,037 --> 01:18:48,997
You gotta be kidding me?

553
01:18:56,172 --> 01:18:59,552
Hey kid, I've got your ball.

554
01:19:06,559 --> 01:19:08,812
Speak, you little bastard.

555
01:19:37,927 --> 01:19:39,680
What are you doing?

556
01:19:42,683 --> 01:19:46,396
Did you know about these?
- What are they?

557
01:19:46,563 --> 01:19:49,232
Why would she draw these?

558
01:19:50,734 --> 01:19:53,570
Those can't be Angela's.

559
01:20:05,876 --> 01:20:07,836
Just in case.

560
01:20:14,219 --> 01:20:15,929
Hey kid, is that you?

561
01:20:19,058 --> 01:20:23,104
What is this thing?
- I don't know.

562
01:20:24,688 --> 01:20:26,358
Whatever it is...

563
01:20:28,110 --> 01:20:29,820
it's real.

564
01:22:27,661 --> 01:22:30,163
What in God's name?

565
01:22:34,585 --> 01:22:36,462
Who are you?

566
01:22:43,595 --> 01:22:47,350
He's gone.

567
01:22:49,394 --> 01:22:55,067
What happened? Are you okay?
- It's too late. It's too late.

568
01:22:56,193 --> 01:22:59,280
Look at this.
- I don't understand. What's going on?

569
01:22:59,447 --> 01:23:03,285
It is the ghost.
- Ghost? What ghost?

570
01:23:03,452 --> 01:23:06,746
From the game.
- Who are you?

571
01:23:06,913 --> 01:23:10,710
You're not Angela's friend.
What do you want from her?

572
01:23:10,877 --> 01:23:14,046
She's suffered enough.
- You get out of here.

573
01:23:14,213 --> 01:23:17,842
Leave the poor girl in peace.
- God sees you, Ms. Channing.

574
01:23:18,010 --> 01:23:20,554
God sees everything.

575
01:23:28,813 --> 01:23:34,445
Who was that lady? And what the hell were you doing
out here in the middle of the freaking night?

576
01:23:35,529 --> 01:23:39,784
It doesn't matter anymore.
They're all gone, it's over.

577
01:23:39,950 --> 01:23:44,122
Sandy, nobody knows where you've been.

578
01:23:46,041 --> 01:23:50,046
If you're in some kind of trouble,
you can talk to me.

579
01:23:50,213 --> 01:23:55,092
It doesn't matter anymore, Eli. It doesn't matter.
- Stop saying that.

580
01:23:59,890 --> 01:24:02,684
It matters to me.

581
01:24:03,769 --> 01:24:08,066
You're my sister, okay.
If something is going on, please tell me.

582
01:24:08,233 --> 01:24:10,276
So I can help you.

583
01:24:11,778 --> 01:24:13,656
You can trust me.

584
01:24:15,032 --> 01:24:19,453
You know that, right?
- I want you to listen to me, okay.

585
01:24:19,620 --> 01:24:24,209
You do know that I love you and
I would never lie to you ever.

586
01:24:24,376 --> 01:24:29,006
But what I'm about tell you is gonna sound
like the craziest thing in the world, because it is.

587
01:24:29,173 --> 01:24:33,344
And I know you're not gonna believe me, because
nobody believes me. But I need you to believe, Eli.

588
01:24:33,511 --> 01:24:35,054
I'm listening.

589
01:24:37,182 --> 01:24:40,936
When we're little, we used to
play games, you remember?

590
01:24:41,103 --> 01:24:45,900
In the graveyard?
- There was a girl, an orphan. Her name was Angela.

591
01:24:47,527 --> 01:24:54,660
Last night we played the game again, but we
weren't alone. Six people are with us, Eli.

592
01:24:54,827 --> 01:25:01,168
Six of our friends, and I know you don't remember them,
but they were there and now they're gone.

593
01:25:02,335 --> 01:25:06,506
Gone? What do you mean gone?
- Something...

594
01:25:06,673 --> 01:25:09,552
This thing took them.

595
01:25:11,429 --> 01:25:16,894
This thing is connected to
Angela and the game?

596
01:25:17,060 --> 01:25:19,021
It has to be.

597
01:25:35,080 --> 01:25:39,836
I knew you wouldn't believe me.
- I believe you.

598
01:25:43,882 --> 01:25:47,720
I believe you.
Why would you make it up?

599
01:25:47,887 --> 01:25:50,139
I wouldn't.

600
01:26:15,626 --> 01:26:21,675
Let's figure this out. The game.
What are the rules of the game?

601
01:26:21,842 --> 01:26:27,265
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven
- Release the one ignored by heaven.

602
01:26:27,431 --> 01:26:29,642
That's Angela, right?

603
01:26:29,809 --> 01:26:34,606
eight, nine, ten, now run and hide
or join her at the devil's side.

604
01:26:34,773 --> 01:26:37,568
That's obvious.

605
01:26:37,734 --> 01:26:43,116
eleven comes, the clock will chime
forgotten souls erased by time.

606
01:26:45,660 --> 01:26:51,375
That's it. Erased. Okay, that's it.
Erased by time. That makes sense now.

607
01:26:51,542 --> 01:26:56,547
Okay, it doesn't make any sense at all,
but I think I know why.

608
01:26:58,758 --> 01:27:04,389
People are gone.
People I knew?

609
01:27:04,556 --> 01:27:09,604
You didn't just know them Eli they were your
best friends and now one by one they've been...

610
01:27:09,770 --> 01:27:11,314
Erased.

611
01:27:16,487 --> 01:27:18,739
Alright, so how does it end? Midnight comes...

612
01:27:18,906 --> 01:27:23,119
It's not too late.
- So kill the ghost or seal your fate.

613
01:27:23,286 --> 01:27:27,207
God, she's still alive. Angela's still alive.

614
01:27:27,373 --> 01:27:30,252
What does that mean?
- It means she has to die.

615
01:27:30,419 --> 01:27:32,046
Who has to die?

616
01:27:33,464 --> 01:27:36,300
What's going on?
- Dad...

617
01:27:38,553 --> 01:27:43,225
We've been really worried about you.
- Step aside, son.

618
01:27:43,391 --> 01:27:46,771
Wait.
- You're sick, honey.

619
01:27:46,938 --> 01:27:51,025
She didn't do anything wrong.
- No, sweetheart. She just needs some help.

620
01:27:51,192 --> 01:27:55,531
No, no. You're not going anywhere, alright. Sit down.
- Let go.

621
01:27:57,032 --> 01:27:59,701
You don't understand, please.

622
01:28:05,166 --> 01:28:10,464
It's gonna be okay, honey.
- You'll get back to normal in no time.

623
01:28:10,631 --> 01:28:13,425
We're gonna take very good
care of you, Ms. Channing.

624
01:28:13,592 --> 01:28:16,346
Sandy, I'm here. I'm right here.
- Step aside.

625
01:28:20,642 --> 01:28:23,228
For Christ's sake. Somebody hold him down.
- Sandy, tell me what to do?

626
01:28:23,395 --> 01:28:28,025
Kill the ghost or seal your fate.
- What is she saying?

627
01:28:28,192 --> 01:28:31,445
Kill her?
- Kill her.

628
01:28:31,612 --> 01:28:33,031
You can't go any further.

629
01:28:35,117 --> 01:28:39,288
I'll do it, Sandy. I'll do it.

630
01:29:07,403 --> 01:29:09,155
Midnight.

631
01:29:11,658 --> 01:29:16,455
Stop. Let me go.
Let me go.

632
01:29:20,084 --> 01:29:25,465
Eli? Where is Eli?
- What is she saying?

633
01:29:25,632 --> 01:29:28,969
Who's Eli, honey?
- Is Eli one of her friends?

634
01:29:30,679 --> 01:29:37,020
Sandy doesn't have any friends.
- Go to sleep, honey. We'll be here when you wake up.

635
01:29:38,772 --> 01:29:40,357
Angela Smith.

636
01:29:44,028 --> 01:29:48,199
That's strange.
Angela Smith is a patient here.

637
01:29:57,709 --> 01:30:00,296
I thought we could play the game?

638
01:30:00,463 --> 01:30:04,425
Who's playing?
- Just us.

639
01:30:18,441 --> 01:30:21,403
I'm sorry about last time.

640
01:30:23,364 --> 01:30:25,867
It's getting late. We should play.

641
01:30:34,960 --> 01:30:40,049
Maybe we shouldn't play.
- No, I want to play.

642
01:30:40,216 --> 01:30:42,468
Wait. Who's the ghost?

643
01:30:44,345 --> 01:30:45,764
You are.

644
01:30:47,141 --> 01:30:52,771
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven
release the one ignored by heaven.

645
01:30:55,233 --> 01:30:57,235
Run.

646
01:31:01,199 --> 01:31:03,367
Help me.

647
01:31:18,092 --> 01:31:19,928
Midnight.

648
01:31:38,823 --> 01:31:41,827
Look at that shit.

649
01:31:59,472 --> 01:32:01,432
Who did this?

650
01:35:10,312 --> 01:35:12,649
I know what I've done...

651
01:35:18,947 --> 01:35:21,867
but I also know what you've done.

652
01:37:46,113 --> 01:37:48,658
You wanna play a game?

653
01:37:51,452 --> 01:37:57,167
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven
release the one ignored by heaven.

654
01:37:57,334 --> 01:38:00,588
eight, nine, ten, now run and hide
or join her at the devil's side.

655
01:38:00,754 --> 01:38:05,760
I remember you. I remember everything.
- Eleven comes, the clock will chime
forgotten souls erased by time.

656
01:38:05,927 --> 01:38:10,140
I'm so sorry.
- Midnight comes, it's not too late
so kill the ghost or seal your fate!

657
01:38:10,307 --> 01:38:13,978
Please. I was your bestfriend.

658
01:38:17,857 --> 01:38:24,281
All I wanted was you.
- I'll never forget you. I promise.

659
01:38:36,253 --> 01:38:39,173
Friends forever. Is that it?

660
01:39:05,202 --> 01:39:07,497
Well look at you.

661
01:39:09,374 --> 01:39:11,000
It's a miracle.

